SUMMARY:Roan Mountain 12.5 mi\, 2\,400 ft  FITNESS HIKE
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis will be an all-day event. It 
 takes a while to get to Roan Mountain. But\, it is worth it\, particularly
  at this time of year\, with the azaleas and rhodos in bloom on the balds.
  We'll meet at the Carver's Gap parking area at 9:30.\n\nHere's the hike w
 e did last year: https://www.alltrails.com/explore/recording/afternoon-bac
 kpack-trip-at-sb6k-south-beyond-6000-and-roan-highlands-618b0ff\n\nLast ye
 ar we were a bit late for some blooms\; this year we'll be 2 weeks earlier
 . As of Sunday afternoon\, temperature forecast looks great\; rain forecas
 t ambiguous.\n\n**Car poolers will meet at the Weaverville Park 'n Ride ne
 xt to exit 17 off I-26 at 8 am.**\n\nPlease let the hike leader know if yo
 u intend to carpool (at 8) or go straight to trailhead (9:30).\n\nAny rain
  cancellation will be made by 6:30 am.\n\nThere exist two brewpubs on the 
 way home in Burnsville.\n\nPACE: Fitness hikes proceed at a steady BRISK p
 ace adjusting for steepness of grade. PLEASE BE IN SHAPE AND CAPABLE OF HI
 KING THIS DISTANCE WITH ELEVATION. We move at 2.5 - 3 mph. This is not a h
 ike for beginners. If your interests include outdoor fitness hiking for ca
 rdio conditioning and endurance join us.\n\nDOGS: Dogs are welcome as long
  as they are trail friendly\, and you bring a leash.\n\nIF YOU SIGN ON THI
 S HIKE AND CHANGE YOU MIND (EVEN IF YOU ARE ON THE WAITLIST) GO BACK TO TH
 E RSVP LINK AND CHANGE YOUR STATUS TO FREE UP YOUR RESERVED SPOT.\n\n*Hike
  Levels:Level 1\; 300-600 feet elevation gain\; Level 2 600-900'\; Level 3
 \, 900-1200"\; Level 4\; 1200-1500' Level 5\; 1500-1800' LEVEL 6\; 1800-21
 00' Level 7*\; 2100-2400' Level 8\; 2400-2700' Level 9\; 2700-3000' Level 
 10\; 3000-4000' ULTIMATE HIKES\; > 4000'\n\nRelease of Liability:\nThe org
 anizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The funct
 ion of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or part
 icipate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agre
 e to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\,
  as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknow
 ledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](h
 ttps://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315140861
 /
