DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T210000
SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nRSVP's don't open until 6PM Sunday night.\nWeather: Rain p
 redicted\, I'll let you know if it's raining\, and/or cancelled.\nI did th
 is hike series for many years before 2022\, but I did it as a high-speed h
 ike\, and I am now doing it as a moderate speed hike. This is a numbers li
 mited event and I expect people who sign-up to show up. Late cancellations
 \, and those that don't show up are bumping other interested hikers\, and 
 they will not be allowed on future hikes.\nIf all goes well\, I will try t
 o post a hike most weeks\, and for days Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start 
 location\, like switching between Hard Times trail-head and Bent Creek Riv
 er Park\, may change.\nThe current route is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks
 \, this is intended as a moderate paced hike\, and we'd like all attendees
  to keep up with the hike leader(s). This hike is intended as a workout hi
 ke for people to get in condition to do weekend hikes.\nModerate paced mea
 ns 22-24 min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\nAs such\, we do not take breaks\, take 
 in views\, or snap photos along the way. Please make sure you're able to k
 eep up with the group. This hike has always served as a good chance to get
  exercise during the week\, meet new people\, and create interest for week
 end enjoyment hikes. It's a great introduction to the AHG family.\nNo need
  to RSVP "No" or "not attending" unless changing from a "Yes."\nPlease rea
 d the full description before RSVPing\, and only sign up if you are sure y
 ou can go. Thanks in advance for keeping your RSVP up-to-date and not bein
 g a last-minute cancellation or no-show. This is an ongoing issue with Mee
 tups and often keeps people on waitlists from being able to attend our hik
 es.\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of
  Brevard Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhatan Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ran
 ch Rd. to Wesley Branch Rd. Follow signs to Lake Powhatan until you come t
 o Hard Times Trailhead on your left\, 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked
 . Parking is very limited at the trailhead but there’s a paved pull-off 
 just before the Hard Times trailhead and more parking just beyond at the L
 edford Branch trailhead. We will access Bent Creek forest by way of Hard T
 imes Trail and do some combination of loop and out and back.\nArrive at th
 e trailhead BY 6:00. Because it is a weeknight hike\, we are unable to wai
 t for latecomers\, fighting daylight.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\
 , please post a comment on this Meetup page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell s
 ervice at the parking lot\, so if we don't have any advance notice of you 
 running late by 5:45\, we can't get any notifications at the trailhead and
  we will not wait for you.\nWe start the hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get m
 uch later than that.\n• Wear closed-toed footwear appropriate for hiking
 . The trail will consist of dirt\, rocks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Bri
 ng plenty of water.\n• Bring rain gear if a chance of rain is in the for
 ecast.\nHeadlamps suggested\n• Dogs on leashes the whole time are welcom
 e. This is an active mountain bike area and it can get messy with dogs run
 ning loose among hikers and mountain bikers.\nPlease make sure to keep you
 r RSVP up-to-date. You don't want to be "that person" who cancels last min
 ute or no-shows and keeps someone from joining in if there's a waitlist. T
 hanks for your consideration - it is appreciated!\nFeel free to post quest
 ions not covered in this description in the comments section.\nThanks - we
 'll see you on the trail!\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis acti
 vity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic and/or natural 
 trails with roots\, rocks\, and steep sections. Participants are responsib
 le for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a
  volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is 
 only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event yo
 u acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of
  injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and as
 sociated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to 
 the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/te
 rms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315137919
 /
